{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfTsxSuoU64ggVvvrPu1T","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Implementation Plan\n\n> Authority note: `request.md`, `manifest.yaml`, and the three named Definition Pack\n> references (`RUNBOOK.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/decisions.md`) were supplied\n> inline and are used as the authority boundary below. The host acknowledged but did\n> **not** return the contents of the component-repository *implementation and test*\n> files I requested (`harness/claude_account_cli.py`, `harness/usage.py`,\n> `harness/agent.py`, `tests/unit/test_usage.py`, `tests/unit/test_claude_account_cli.py`,\n> `tests/unit/test_live_tier.py`, `tests/live/test_live_eval.py`). I do not claim to have\n> read them; every place where their current internals matter is recorded as a Planning\n> gap and the executor must confirm the exact symbols/assertions before editing.\n\n## Bounded objective\n\nMake the `claude_account` adapter (ADR-019) capture the Claude CLI's **actual** token\nusage from `claude --print --output-format json` — the aggregate token quartet\n(`input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `cache_read_input_tokens`,\n`cache_creation_input_tokens`) plus the per-model `modelUsage` breakdown, including\nhelper-model entries — and record it through the existing telemetry path (ADR-005),\n**without persisting or logging the CLI's raw response body or any credential material**\n(ADR-019). Secondary, in-scope because manifest concern **C1** ties it to this change:\ncorrect the now-stale `RUNBOOK.md` statement that the Claude CLI does not expose cache\ncounters, and reconcile the parallel claim in `docs/decisions.md` (ADR-018).\n\nExplicitly out of scope: metered USD pricing for the account plan (ADR-018/019 keep this\nabsent; the harness \"does not manufacture a `$0` cost\"), the `anthropic_sdk` path, and any\nchange to evidence-tool behaviour.\n\n## Definition Pack interpretation\n\n- **ADR-005** (`docs/decisions.md`): telemetry is one JSONL line per LLM request + one\n  run-summary line; the record already models a \"token quartet, USD, latency, cache\n  hits\"; `record_run()` **never raises**; new columns are added via a `schema_version`\n  bump. New cache/per-model fields must follow this shape and preserve the non-raising\n  guarantee.\n- **ADR-006 / architecture §8**: the cache regression check is `cache_read_tokens > 0`\n  in usage telemetry. For that check to mean anything on the account path, the adapter\n  must actually populate `cache_read_tokens`.\n- **ADR-018**: asserts \"Account plans expose neither per-request USD pricing nor provider\n  cache counters through this CLI boundary\" and that the harness \"skips only the\n  Anthropic-specific cache-counter assertion.\" **ADR-019** supersedes ADR-018 for the\n  provider choice but repeats \"Claude CLI owns subscription limits and cache behavior, so\n  the harness reports account-plan usage.\"\n- **Concern C1** + **request.md**: `claude 2.1.168 --print --output-format json` *does*\n  return `usage.cache_read_input_tokens` / `cache_creation_input_tokens` and per-model\n  `modelUsage` (verified 2026-09-27). This directly contradicts the ADR-018 premise; the\n  request treats the counters as available and requires recording them. Helper-model\n  `modelUsage` entries are \"not yet observed\" — the request asks to record them but no\n  captured sample defines their shape.\n- **\"Without exposing raw responses or credentials\"**: the `--output-format json`\n  envelope carries the model's generated text and possibly session metadata; only the\n  `usage`/`modelUsage` numbers may enter telemetry. ADR-019 already forbids printing any\n  part of the token; that posture extends to the parsed JSON.\n\n## Current implementation\n\nInferred from the Definition Packs (not from source, which was not returned):\n\n- `harness/claude_account_cli.py` is the ADR-019 Pydantic-AI adapter that invokes\n  `claude --print` with structured output, disabled tools/MCP, a scrubbed child\n  environment, and requires `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`. It currently reports \"account-plan\n  usage\" but, per RUNBOOK §1 and ADR-018, does **not** capture cache counters or a\n  per-model breakdown.\n- `harness/usage.py` owns the JSONL append, `spend_usd()`, `record_run()`, and the\n  DuckDB read-time views (`sql/usage_views.sql`); it defines the usage record schema and\n  the `schema_version`.\n- `harness/agent.py` wires per-request/run telemetry.\n- `RUNBOOK.md` §1 states: \"The Anthropic SDK-only cache-counter test is skipped because\n  Claude CLI does not expose those counters\" — the line concern C1 flags as stale.\n- A cache-counter assertion is currently **skipped** on the account path (ADR-018);\n  its location (unit vs live tier) was not confirmable.\n\n## Proposed changes\n\nFiles and the responsibility of each change. Test/enforcement files are listed with what\neach must gain; anything omitted here is out of scope for the executor.\n\n1. **`harness/claude_account_cli.py`** — request `--output-format json`; parse the\n   `usage` aggregate (four token fields) and the `modelUsage` map (per model, including\n   helper-model entries); surface these as a structured usage object to the agent loop.\n   Ensure the raw response text and any session/credential-bearing fields are dropped\n   before anything is logged or recorded.\n2. **`harness/usage.py`** — extend the usage record schema to carry\n   `cache_read_input_tokens`, `cache_creation_input_tokens`, and a per-model breakdown\n   (aggregate + `modelUsage` incl. helper models), with a `schema_version` bump per\n   ADR-005; preserve `record_run()` non-raising behaviour when fields are absent (older\n   records / SDK path).\n3. **`harness/agent.py`** — populate the telemetry record from the adapter's parsed usage\n   on the `claude_account` branch (aggregate + per-model), leaving the SDK path unchanged.\n4. **`sql/usage_views.sql`** — expose the new cache and per-model columns if the views\n   enumerate columns explicitly (so the ADR-006 `cache_read_tokens > 0` regression query\n   and per-model reporting resolve on the account path).\n5. **`RUNBOOK.md`** — correct the line concern C1 names (the \"Claude CLI does not expose\n   those counters\" claim and the associated skipped-test sentence); state that\n   `--output-format json` now reports cache and per-model usage.\n6. **`docs/decisions.md`** — append a new ADR (append-only log) recording that the Claude\n   CLI now exposes cache and per-model `modelUsage`, superseding the ADR-018 premise for\n   the account path; note helper-model entries are recorded when present but were not yet\n   observed. **Authority-sensitive** (see Planning gaps).\n\nEnforcing tests / invariants (executor must confirm current contents, which were not\nreturned):\n\n- **`tests/unit/test_usage.py`** — must gain: round-trip of the new cache and per-model\n  fields through JSONL append → DuckDB views; the `cache_read_tokens > 0` regression\n  query resolving against an account-path record; `record_run()` still not raising when\n  the new fields are missing (schema-version compatibility).\n- **`tests/unit/test_claude_account_cli.py`** — must gain: parsing a representative\n  `--output-format json` payload into the usage object (aggregate + `modelUsage`,\n  including a helper-model entry once a shape is fixed); a negative assertion that the raw\n  response body and credential material never enter the record or logs.\n- **`tests/unit/test_live_tier.py`** and/or **`tests/live/test_live_eval.py`** — the\n  cache-counter assertion currently **skipped** on the account path (RUNBOOK §1) must be\n  un-skipped or re-scoped so it enforces cache-counter capture on `claude_account`. The\n  executor must locate which of these holds the skip and update it; leaving the skip in\n  place would leave the invariant unenforced and is not permitted by this plan.\n- **`tests/unit/test_settings_secrets.py`** — touch only if a new setting/env var is\n  introduced (not anticipated); named here so the executor checks rather than assumes.\n\n## Verification approach\n\n- Repository verify command (manifest): `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q`.\n- Focused deterministic runs: `test_usage.py`, `test_claude_account_cli.py`, and the\n  updated cache-counter test — driven by a **captured** `--output-format json` fixture so\n  the parse is deterministic and offline (per ADR-016, offline completeness is silence\n  about the live path, so the fixture must come from a real capture, not invention).\n- Acceptance cases: (a) a JSON payload with cache and multi-model `modelUsage` produces a\n  record carrying all four token fields and per-model rows; (b) the ADR-006 cache\n  regression query returns `cache_read_tokens > 0`; (c) the raw response text/credentials\n  do not appear in the JSONL record or logs; (d) an SDK-path record still validates\n  (schema-version back-compat).\n- Live tier remains manual (`python -m evals.live`, `tests/live/`), not a PR gate.\n\n## Risks, assumptions and gaps\n\n- **Assumption**: the CLI `usage`/`modelUsage` field names match those in concern C1\n  (`cache_read_input_tokens`, `cache_creation_input_tokens`, `modelUsage`); a captured\n  sample must confirm exact keys before coding.\n- **Risk**: helper-model `modelUsage` shape is unobserved; recording it against a guessed\n  shape reproduces the O-6 failure mode (inventing a payload). Prefer a defensive parse\n  that records whatever `modelUsage` entries appear without hardcoding a helper schema.\n- **Risk**: `docs/decisions.md` / `RUNBOOK.md` edits change vendored Definition Pack\n  content whose `authority` is `null` in the manifest — no designated approver.\n- **Risk**: a `schema_version` bump can affect downstream consumers of the usage JSONL;\n  no captured consumer baseline is available.\n- **Assumption**: `sql/usage_views.sql` enumerates columns; if it selects `*`, item 4 may\n  be a no-op.\n\n## Planning gaps\n\nGAP: docs/decisions.md ADR-018 states the Claude CLI exposes no cache counters over the CLI boundary, but request.md and manifest concern C1 require recording them — vendored authority vs request/observed CLI behaviour conflict.\nGAP: request.md requires recording helper-model usage, but manifest concern C1 records helper-model `modelUsage` entries as \"not yet observed\" — no captured sample defines the shape (definition insufficiency).\nGAP: manifest `definitions[].authority` is null for RUNBOOK.md, docs/architecture.md and docs/decisions.md — no designated authority to approve superseding ADR-018 or editing the RUNBOOK line.\nGAP: host did not return contents of harness/claude_account_cli.py, harness/usage.py, harness/agent.py, tests/unit/test_usage.py, tests/unit/test_claude_account_cli.py, tests/unit/test_live_tier.py, tests/live/test_live_eval.py — exact symbols and the location of the skipped cache-counter test are unconfirmed (source vs plan).\nGAP: \"without exposing raw responses\" is undefined against a field schema — request.md gives no enumeration of which `--output-format json` fields count as raw response vs recordable telemetry.\nGAP: ADR-005 prescribes a `schema_version` bump for new fields, but manifest `compatibility.affected_consumers` is empty — no baseline of usage-JSONL consumers to check the bump against.\n\n## Size estimate\n\nMedium. The core change is a bounded parse-and-record addition on one adapter plus a\nschema extension in the usage module, wired at one call site, with matching test updates\nand two documentation corrections. It is not small because it crosses the adapter,\ntelemetry schema, DuckDB views, three-to-four test files (including un-skipping a live\ninvariant), and two vendored Definition Pack documents; it is not large because no new\nsubsystem, contract version, or evidence-path behaviour changes. Confidence is limited by\nthe unread implementation/test files and the unobserved helper-model shape (se