{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfTtHxb2v51RGSXSECmsC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Implementation Plan\n\n## Bounded objective\nMake the Claude subscription-account transport (`harness/claude_account_cli.py`) populate the `RequestUsage` on the `ModelResponse` it returns so that the harness's existing telemetry (`harness/usage.py`, ADR-005) records the Claude CLI's **actual** token usage — aggregate input/output plus `cache_read`/`cache_write`, and the per-model breakdown reported in the CLI's `modelUsage` (including any helper-model entry) — while continuing to emit no raw CLI response body and no credential/token. Also correct the now-stale statement in `RUNBOOK.md` that \"Claude CLI does not expose cache counters.\"\n\nToday the adapter returns `ModelResponse(parts=[ToolCallPart(...)], model_name=…, provider_name=\"claude-account\", finish_reason=\"tool_call\")` with **no `usage=`**, so every account-mode request is recorded as all-zero tokens and the cache-hit regression view (ADR-006) can never fire in the local POC path. This is the whole gap.\n\nThis is a small, well-bounded change against one adapter plus its enforcing unit test and one doc line. It is **not** a change to the usage schema, the DuckDB views, or the cost model.\n\n## Definition Pack interpretation\nThree Definition Pack references are pinned in the manifest, all in `k-12Harness`:\n- **RUNBOOK.md** — §1 says the SDK-only cache-counter live test \"is skipped because Claude CLI does not expose those counters.\" Concern C1 records this as stale for `claude 2.1.168`. This line is in scope to correct.\n- **docs/architecture.md** — §9 (carried invariants) and the contract boundary; ADR references. It states telemetry is \"one JSONL line per LLM request + one per run\" read through DuckDB. Nothing here forbids populating account-mode usage; it constrains the *shape* (one request line, token quartet, cache hits).\n- **docs/decisions.md** — ADR-005 (usage/cost telemetry, JSONL + DuckDB), ADR-006 (cache regression = `cache_read_tokens > 0`), ADR-018 and ADR-019 (account transport). **ADR-018 explicitly asserts \"Account plans expose neither per-request USD pricing nor provider cache counters through this CLI boundary,\"** which directly contradicts the request and C1. `docs/decisions.md` is declared append-only, so this contradiction cannot be edited away in place — it must be resolved by authority (see Planning gaps).\n\nThe token convention is authoritative in `harness/usage.py` and its test: pydantic-ai's `RequestUsage` follows genai-prices where `input_tokens` **includes** cache read+write, whereas Anthropic/CLI reports `input_tokens` **excluding** cache. Any mapping the plan adds must obey that convention (the `USAGE_SONNET` example in `tests/unit/test_usage.py`: 1000 uncached + 2000 read + 100 write ⇒ `input_tokens=3100`).\n\n## Current implementation\n- `harness/claude_account_cli.py::_invoke_claude` decodes the CLI stdout twice (`_raise_for_result_error` → `_result_envelope`, then `_structured_action`) and builds a `ModelResponse` with no usage. `_structured_action`/`_result_envelope` already decode the top-level JSON envelope; the CLI envelope is known (from `tests/unit/test_claude_account_cli.py::test_session_limit_…`) to carry a top-level `usage` block (e.g. `cache_creation_input_tokens`). C1 asserts it also carries `cache_read_input_tokens`, `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, and a per-model `modelUsage` map.\n- `harness/usage.py` already reads `message.usage.input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `cache_read_tokens`, `cache_write_tokens`, and `details = dict(message.usage.details or {})` into `LlmRequestRecord`, and sums them into `RunSummaryRecord`. It needs **no change** to record account usage once the adapter supplies a populated `RequestUsage`. `LlmRequestRecord` has a single `model` column (`SCHEMA_VERSION = 1`); per-model breakdown has no first-class column and would be carried in `details`.\n- `harness/agent.py::_finish` already records the run via `usage.record_run` on every branch, so no agent change is required.\n- Live tests encode the stale assumption in code: `tests/live/test_live_eval.py::test_the_frozen_prompt_is_actually_cached` skips for `claude_account`, and `test_a_live_run_stays_inside_the_control_envelope` asserts `not complete` (cost unpriced — still true; tokens ≠ cost).\n\n## Proposed changes\n- **`harness/claude_account_cli.py`** — the substantive change.\n  - Add a pure helper, e.g. `_request_usage(envelope: dict) -> RequestUsage`, that:\n    - Reads the top-level `usage` block: maps `cache_read_input_tokens → cache_read_tokens`, `cache_creation_input_tokens → cache_write_tokens`, `output_tokens → output_tokens`, and sets `input_tokens = usage.input_tokens + cache_read + cache_write` to honour the genai-prices convention that `usage.py` and `test_usage.py` assume.\n    - Reads the per-model `modelUsage` map (main model + any helper model). Aggregates its token counts into the returned `RequestUsage` totals when present (so helper-model tokens enter the aggregate), and records the per-model breakdown as **integers-only** entries in `RequestUsage.details` (keyed by model name, e.g. `{\"modelUsage.<model>.input_tokens\": n, …}`), which `usage.py` copies verbatim into `LlmRequestRecord.details`.\n    - Tolerates a missing/partial `usage` block by returning zeroed usage rather than raising (a run must not fail on telemetry parsing).\n    - Emits **only numeric token counts and model-name keys** — never the CLI `result` text, never any credential/token.\n  - Refactor `_invoke_claude` to decode the success envelope once and pass `usage=_request_usage(envelope)` into the returned `ModelResponse` (reuse the same decoded dict for `_structured_action`). No behavioural change to the action-extraction or error paths.\n  - Keep `_redact_account_token` on every error string path (unchanged).\n- **`tests/unit/test_claude_account_cli.py`** — this is the coverage/enforcement file for the adapter; every helper in the module already has a dedicated unit test, so the new symbol must gain the same. It must gain:\n  - A test that a success envelope's `usage` block maps into `RequestUsage` with cache read/write set and `input_tokens` including cache (mirroring the convention in `test_usage.py`).\n  - A test that `modelUsage` with a main model **and a helper model** produces an aggregate that sums both and a `details` breakdown carrying each model's numeric counts.\n  - A test that the parser emits no raw `result` text and no account token in `usage`/`details` (redaction/no-raw-leak invariant).\n  - A test that a missing/empty `usage` block yields zero usage without raising.\n  - (Recommended) extend `test_account_model_has_no_http_provider` neighbourhood so `build_claude_account_model` end-to-end still returns a `ModelResponse` whose `usage` is populated when the fake CLI returns a usage block.\n- **`harness/usage.py`** — **no code change**; it already surfaces the four token fields and `details`. `tests/unit/test_usage.py` is the enforcing invariant for the token convention our mapping must satisfy and **must remain green unchanged** — the adapter mapping is written to agree with it (it is the reason `input_tokens` is summed rather than passed through).\n- **`RUNBOOK.md`** — correct the §1 sentence that says the cache-counter test is skipped \"because Claude CLI does not expose those counters\" to reflect that `claude` now returns `cache_read_input_tokens`/`cache_creation_input_tokens` and per-model `modelUsage`, and that the harness now records them (per C1).\n\nFlagged-but-out-of-core-scope (do not implement around them silently — see gaps):\n- `tests/live/test_live_eval.py` — the `test_the_frozen_prompt_is_actually_cached` skip and the `not complete` assertion encode the same stale claim as RUNBOOK:55. Reconciling the skip is a live-tier behavioural decision and is left out of this scope unless authority confirms cache-read is reliably reported in account mode; naming it here so it is not implemented around.\n- `docs/decisions.md` — ADR-018's cache-counter claim conflicts with the request; resolving it is an append-only ADR addition (authority decision), not part of this bounded code change.\n- `releases/_next/` release note — the repo carries a release-notes CI gate (`.github/workflows/pr-checks.yml`, `.claude/hooks/require-release-notes.sh`); a note may be a required artifact (unconfirmed this session).\n\n## Verification approach\n- Deterministic, offline: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_claude_account_cli.py -q` (new usage-parsing tests) and `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_usage.py -q` (must stay green, proving the convention held).\n- Full suite (manifest `verify`): `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q`.\n- Acceptance case: a fake CLI success envelope carrying `usage` + `modelUsage` produces a `ModelResponse` whose `usage` has non-zero `input_tokens`/`output_tokens`/`cache_read_tokens`/`cache_write_tokens`; through `usage.extract_request_records` the resulting `LlmRequestRecord` shows those values and a `details` per-model breakdown, and neither the record nor `details` contains the CLI `result` text or the account token.\n- Live tier (`tests/live`, `-m live`, manual, never a PR gate): not required to pass for this change; any decision to enable the account-mode cache-read assertion is gated on the helper-model/cache-read gaps below.\n\n## Risks, assumptions and gaps\n- Assumption: the CLI top-level `usage` block uses Anthropic-style field names (`input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `cache_read_input_tokens`, `cache_creation_input_tokens`) reporting input **excluding** cache, per C1. Only `cache_creation_input_tokens` is confirmed by an existing repo fixture; the rest are asserted by C1, not pinned.\n- Assumption: `modelUsage` is a map keyed by model name with per-model token counts; the helper-model entry shape is unobserved (C1).\n- Risk: if `modelUsage` totals and the top-level `usage` block can disagree, the plan must pick one as the aggregate source; the plan uses `modelUsage` sum when present, else the top-level block, and records both signals in `details` for auditability.\n- Risk: recording per-model usage only in `details` (not as columns/rows) may not satisfy a stricter reading of \"per-model\"; a first-class column would be a `SCHEMA_VERSION` bump (larger scope).\n- Telemetry-never-fails posture (ADR-005) is preserved by making the parser total-tolerant and by `record_run` already swallowing errors.\n\n## Planning gaps\nGAP: request.md (\"record … cache and helper-model usage\") vs docs/decisions.md ADR-018 (\"Account plans expose neither per-request USD pricing nor provider cache counters through this CLI boundary\") — ADR asserts the counters are unavailable; append-only ADR log needs a superseding decision to authorise recording them.\nGAP: request.md (\"helper-model usage\") vs manifest concern C1 (\"Helper-model entries in modelUsage not yet observed\") — no captured sample of a helper-model `modelUsage` entry, so its exact keys/shape are unverified.\nGAP: exact CLI `usage`/`modelUsage` field names — only `usage.cache_creation_input_tokens` is pinned by a repo fixture (tests/unit/test_claude_account_cli.py); `cache_read_input_tokens`, `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, and the `modelUsage` structure are asserted only by concern C1 and not captured under work-store evidence.\nGAP: per-model granularity — request.md implies per-model recording but harness/usage.py `LlmRequestRecord` (SCHEMA_VERSION=1) has a single `model` column; unresolved whether `details`-dict capture satisfies the request or a schema_version bump is required (ADR-005 designs bumps in).\nGAP: RUNBOOK.md:55 skip rationale vs tests/live/test_live_eval.py (`test_the_frozen_prompt_is_actually_cached` skip and `test_a_live_run_stays_inside_the_control_envelope` `not complete` assertion) — both encode \"account mode does not expose cache counters\"; unresolved whether the live cache-read assertion should now be enabled for account mode.\nGAP: release-notes CI invariant (.github/workflows/pr-checks.yml / .claude/hooks/require-release-notes.sh) could not be read this session — unconfirmed whether a releases/_next note is a required artifact for this change.\n\n## Size estimate\nSmall: the substantive change is one helper plus a two-line refactor in `harness/claude_account_cli.py`, its enforcing unit tests in `tests/unit/test_claude_account_cli.py`, and one corrected sentence in `RUNBOOK.md`; `harness/usage.py` and the DuckDB views are unchanged and merely inherit the populated usage. It grows toward medium only if authority requires the ADR-018 superseding decision, the live-tier reconciliation, or a per-model schema bump — each of which is deferred as a gap rather than folded in.\n\n```yaml\nsize_estimate:\n  files: 3\n  scale: small\n  subsystems: [harness, tests, docs]\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":556,"cache_read_input_tokens":98313,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":556},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8258a59e-8fe5-45f6-84ca-bc7d6860cc83","uuid":"0a4dc35f-3b6e-4c79-93b2-2dc6ed787c40","request_id":"req_011CfTtHxDhMHudftic1jMnc"}
