{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfTtWKGZXnsuQA7Xu8vcH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've completed the bounded implementation plan. Summary of what it establishes:\n\n- **Objective**: populate `RequestUsage` on the `ModelResponse` returned by `harness/claude_account_cli.py::_invoke_claude` so the existing `harness/usage.py` telemetry records the CLI's real aggregate + per-model (incl. helper-model and cache) token usage, and correct the stale RUNBOOK line — without leaking raw responses or the token.\n- **Key finding**: the adapter currently returns a `ModelResponse` with no `usage=`, so account-mode requests record all-zero tokens; `usage.py` already reads the token quartet and `details`, so it needs **no change** (its `test_usage.py` token convention is the invariant the new mapping must honour).\n- **Scoped files**: `harness/claude_account_cli.py` (new `_request_usage` helper + one-line wiring), `tests/unit/test_claude_account_cli.py` (the enforcing coverage file — must gain cache/helper-model/no-leak/robustness tests), `RUNBOOK.md` (correct the cache-counter line).\n- **Recorded conflicts as GAPs**, notably the direct contradiction between the request and ADR-018 (append-only), the unobserved helper-model `modelUsage` shape, the single-`model`-column schema limit on \"per-model\", and the live-test/RUNBOOK skip reconciliation.\n\nNote: I was unable to read `.github/workflows/pr-checks.yml` and `.claude/hooks/require-release-notes.sh` this session, so the release-notes CI requirement is flagged as an unconfirmed gap rather than asserted."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13875,"cache_read_input_tokens":98869,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13875},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"