{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfTtapw8WEBHtwBPo7wfc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've completed the bounded implementation plan for work item 20260908T113226. \n\nThe plan centers on the single real gap: `harness/claude_account_cli.py::_invoke_claude` builds its `ModelResponse` with no `usage=`, so the existing ADR-005 telemetry records all-zero tokens for every account-mode request. The fix is a pure `_request_usage()` helper that maps the CLI's success-envelope `usage`/`modelUsage` block into a `RequestUsage` obeying the genai-prices convention already assumed by `harness/usage.py` and `test_usage.py` (input includes cache), aggregating helper-model counts and recording the per-model breakdown in `details` — emitting only numeric counts and model names, never raw response text or the token.\n\nKey scoping decisions surfaced as structured gaps rather than expanded scope:\n- **ADR-018 contradiction** — it asserts account plans expose no cache counters; the append-only ADR log needs a superseding decision, not an edit.\n- **Unobserved helper-model shape** and **unpinned field names** — only `cache_creation_input_tokens` is confirmed by an existing fixture; the rest rest on concern C1.\n- **Per-model granularity** — `LlmRequestRecord` (SCHEMA_VERSION=1) has one `model` column; whether `details` capture suffices or a schema bump is needed is left unresolved.\n- **Live-tier reconciliation** — the RUNBOOK skip rationale and two live tests encode the same stale claim.\n\nI also confirmed the release-notes CI gate (which I could only inspect after the host provided the file bodies), so a `releases/_next/*.md` note is a mandated fourth file rather than an open question."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4974,"cache_read_input_tokens":102490,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephe